  "interpretation": {
    "ṛgveda": "The Zürich lemma avata- is dental throughout its 20 tokens. The longer nominative plural avatāsaḥ has Vedic asuk under 7.1.50.",
    "white_yajurveda": "At VSM 11.61a the pit is addressed, avaṭa. ŚBM 6.5.4.3 repeats the vocative in the mantra and immediately uses the same stem in the nominative of the prose explanation. The two Brāhmaṇa locative singular passages give the same pouring formula at distinct ritual locations.",
    "source_separation": "The eight retroflex occurrences populate five previously written positions. The oral quotation connects the Saṃhitā and Brāhmaṇa; their two locators are not two independent morphological proofs. The retroflex dental contrast does not license substituting one technical affix name for another."
  },
